==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|val}} (declined {{m|gmh|valwe}}), from {{inh|de|goh|falo}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*falwaz}}. Doublet of {{m|gmh|falb}} (“fair”, of a horse), from the Middle High German inflected stem. The form {{m|de||fahl}} is based on the uninflected stem. However, the lengthened vowel points to influence by varieties that reduce ''-lw-'' to ''-l-'' even in open syllables; these include {{der|de|gml|vāl}} (declined {{m|gml|vāle}}), from {{der|de|osx|falu}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|vaal}}.

